# Every script here runs on Linux. Checked out with CRLF endings they fail in
# ways that do not look like line-ending problems: bash reports
# "$'\r': command not found", a `cd` into a path with a trailing \r fails, and
# the driver then prints its headers and silently measures nothing. Forcing LF
# on checkout keeps that from happening on a Windows clone.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
